    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Rhonda Shader is a former Placentia city councilmember and mayor, and owns an insurance agency. She was first elected in 2016 and has served on the St. Jude Medical Center Community Health Committee and the Orange County Human Relations Commission. Her campaign says that as mayor, she launched an independent fire department, saving the city over $28 million, and created a city-county infrastructure district that generated 5,000 jobs. In 2022, she opposed raising the minimum wage and supported overturning laws she said enabled smash-and-grab robberies. During her 2022 campaign, she proposed lowering the gas tax and sales tax.",
